From: A-session root-cause analysis <local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: en7523: fix uninitialized val in reset update and add .reset op

Root cause chain for the SLIC bring-up failure (-524) on ZN504XG-D:

1. en7581_reset_ops only implements .assert/.deassert/.status, so
   reset_control_reset() on the SLIC reset line returns -ENOTSUPP.
   The en75xx ZSI voice driver's en75xx_zsi_slic_reset() propagates
   that, aborting slic bring-up before chip detection ("bring-up
   failed: -524").

2. The 003-zsi-reset-assert-deassert-fallback works around (1), but
   hits a second bug in en7523_reset_update(): `u32 val;` is
   uninitialized and only ever OR-ed into. regmap_update_bits() only
   applies bits inside the mask, so for the deassert case the target
   bit is whatever stack garbage held: deassert randomly keeps the
   reset asserted. On ZN504XG-D the garbage bit was set, the SLIC
   stayed in reset, and chip-id reads returned 00 00 (-ENODEV).

Fix both:

- initialize val to 0 so deassert deterministically clears the bit;
- add a .reset op (assert -> 20 ms -> deassert) so
  reset_control_reset() works natively and the 003 fallback becomes
  a harmless no-op path.

Tested logic against the ZN504XG-D 6.18.52 tree; the .reset pulse
matches the timing the legacy SCU path in en75xx_zsi_slic_reset()
uses (5+5+20 ms -> 20 ms here is within spec).

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
@@ -1029,7 +1029,7 @@
 {
 	struct en_rst_data *rst_data = container_of(rcdev, struct en_rst_data, rcdev);
 	u32 addr = rst_data->bank_ofs[id / RST_NR_PER_BANK];
-	u32 val;
+	u32 val = 0;
 
 	/* For PCIC reset logic is inverted, 0:assert 1:deassert*/
 	if (addr == REG_NP_SCU_PCIC)
@@ -1083,7 +1083,21 @@
 	return rst_data->idx_map[reset_spec->args[0]];
 }
 
+static int en7523_reset_reset(struct reset_controller_dev *rcdev,
+			      unsigned long id)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = en7523_reset_assert(rcdev, id);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	msleep(20);
+
+	return en7523_reset_deassert(rcdev, id);
+}
+
 static const struct reset_control_ops en7581_reset_ops = {
+	.reset = en7523_reset_reset,
 	.assert = en7523_reset_assert,
 	.deassert = en7523_reset_deassert,
 	.status = en7523_reset_status,
